      "id": 496172,
      "username": "jaymez",
      "name": null,
      "created_at": "2026-03-21T10:30:27.088Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I’d like to understand what’s the logics thought about as it is now <img src=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/images/emoji/twitter/thinking.png?v=15\" title=\":thinking:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":thinking:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n<p>I thought the developers considered the option if the invoice was not paid, and that is good. But why is not possible deactivate ‘Update Outstanding for Self‘ when, for instance, it is about an already paid invoice <img src=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/images/emoji/twitter/man_shrugging.png?v=15\" title=\":man_shrugging:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":man_shrugging:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"> ?</p>\n<p>I’d like to know how master users make settings when they are in my situation</p>",
