      "id": 496178,
      "username": "trustedcomputer",
      "name": "Ben Erickson",
      "created_at": "2026-03-21T15:22:07.838Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Me too. Here’s what I’ve started doing as a workaround.</p>\n<p>Start from the purchase invoice that needs to have a return. Create a return/debit note from there, which copies all the relevant items and data from the original purchase invoice into the return purchase invoice. Toggle “is return” off and then back on and uncheck “Update Billed Amount in Purchase Receipt”, which unlinks the return invoice from the returned invoice completely. This way all of the accounting stays straight at least, but I lose the link between the returned invoice and the return invoice. I am sure there must be a better way.</p>",
